{
  "name": "Prepare support replies with a Straitly AI Agent, Gmail and a shared FAQ",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "532ccfa7-5436-48c1-9b9b-a28c37f08dfe",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -656,
        -256
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Prepare support replies with a Straitly AI Agent, Gmail and a shared FAQ\n\nKeep support replies in Gmail drafts for a teammate to review. A read-only FAQ tool grounds the AI Agent, while a prepaid-balance check keeps the workflow from starting a model run when funds are low.\n\n### How it works\n1. **Watch Inbox** picks up one unread inbox email per poll. **Config** keeps IDs, thresholds and model settings together.\n2. **Read Ledger** and **Plan Intake** reject malformed input, skip automated senders and suppress message IDs already recorded.\n3. **Claim Message** records processing before any AI or draft action. **Check Balance** blocks AI spending below the configured floor.\n4. **Triage Email** uses **Straitly Model**, **Read FAQ** and **Reply Schema** to propose a classified reply. **Check Reply** checks citations against tool observations.\n5. **Create Draft** saves an approved answer in its existing Gmail thread. **Label Email** marks categories or human review. No node sends email.\n6. **Save Outcome** keeps the result. **Alert Team** flags urgent messages and the first low-balance hold of each local day.\n7. **Daily Digest** reads yesterday's counts and checks sent Gmail messages before listing unanswered urgent threads.\n\n### Setup\n- [ ] Install independent community package n8n-nodes-straitly on self-hosted n8n. Community nodes are unavailable on n8n Cloud until verified. Attach a Straitly API credential.\n- [ ] Attach Gmail OAuth2 to trigger, drafts, labels and sent-message reads.\n- [ ] Attach Google Sheets OAuth2. Create FAQ and Log tabs using the documented column names.\n- [ ] Attach Slack credentials and invite the bot to the configured channel.\n- [ ] Replace all sheet, channel and Gmail label IDs in Config.\n- [ ] Set instance production concurrency to one and use one active workflow copy. Sheets claims are not atomic locks.\n\n### Customization\n- Adjust minimum balance and confidence in Config. The balance floor is not a hard request cost cap.\n- Change the model and token allowance in Config.\n- Keep FAQ answers approved and concise.\n- Change the daily schedule and workflow timezone together; review processing claims manually before replaying failed executions.",
        "width": 560,
        "height": 1304
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "b72a0812-d16c-431c-a536-eb8568d84d35",
      "name": "1. Inbox and routing",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -48,
        -256
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 1. Inbox and routing\n\nTwo triggers share one configuration. Inbox polling deliberately handles one message at a time; daily executions take the digest branch without running the AI Agent.",
        "width": 776,
        "height": 704,
        "color": 7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "5b5ac42e-474f-4895-924d-2ce28f91fd7e",
      "name": "2. Claims and budget",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        744,
        -256
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 2. Claims and budget\n\nRead the durable ledger before doing work. Existing message IDs stop here. Processing claims prevent whole-execution replays from creating another draft after a crash.",
        "width": 1448,
        "height": 704,
        "color": 7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "e955c120-852c-469f-9388-2c8f05ea981b",
      "name": "3. Grounded draft proposal",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        2208,
        -256
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 3. Grounded draft proposal\n\nThe agent reads approved FAQ rows through a read-only tool. Defensive checks reject malformed output and unknown citations; unsupported answers stay with a human.",
        "width": 1000,
        "height": 1104,
        "color": 7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "6393416b-1548-4ad3-a867-9a2b39753a59",
      "name": "4. Labels and durable outcomes",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -48,
        896
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 4. Labels and durable outcomes\n\nHuman-review labels cover budget holds and failed proposals. Label failures stay visible in the saved status, and drafts remain unsent for a teammate to inspect.",
        "width": 1896,
        "height": 704,
        "color": 7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "abc5a695-f3b6-4966-a32f-cc44a52357a6",
      "name": "5. Daily follow-up",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -48,
        1648
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 5. Daily follow-up\n\nRead yesterday in the configured timezone, count category and status pairs and compare urgent threads against later sent messages. Empty days still produce a digest.",
        "width": 1000,
        "height": 504,
        "color": 7
      }
    },
